WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:02.802 line:0%
-I command you!

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.737 line:0%
-Why should we listen to you?

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.105 line:0%
[ Crowd shouting ]

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.308 line:0%
-Because I...am...God!

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:12.111 line:0%
[ All gasping, shouting ]

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:17.983 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:20.820
-So, you play God.
-Yes.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.956
There was -- there was a thing
on that robe, on that cape,

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:26.625
though, that was not safe
for television, I don't think.

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:28.327
-Oh, really?
-But, great!

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:31.564
-Go back,
rewind and pause, kids.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.566
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.401
I think we would've
got away with it, Bowen.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:36.736
-Damn!
-Oh.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.138
-Sorry, Standards and Practices.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:40.640
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.974
-Well, guess what.

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:44.043
It was hard finding a clip
from "Dicks: The Musical."

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.246
-I know, I'm sure.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.580
-We didn't want
to have you on here

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.048
and show a 2 1/2-second clip.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.317
-Sure. You couldn't
have called it...

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.319
I can't -- I can't even come up
with an alternative

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.154
to "Dicks: The Musical"
that is safe for television.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:57.157
-This was a UCB show

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.391
that you were involved with
back in 2014?

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:01.894
-I was not involved.
I was just, like, a lowly,

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:03.897
lowly audience member.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.065
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:09.235
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.904
I was, but I saw it like
multiple times.

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:14.707
And it was -- this was,
like, back in 2014, 2015.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.609
And it was Josh Sharp
and Aaron Jackson

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.778
who are in the movie
who play these twin brothers.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:22.315
It's a gay "Parent Trap,"
basically, that's a musical.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.884
And, but then they did
this show like once a month

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.286
and then it became
this, like, meeting ground

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:29.522
and this touchpoint for a lot
of queer comedians in the city,

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.223
like, who had never
really talked

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:32.659
to each other before that,

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:34.193
who didn't hang out,
and it was -- it was great.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.928
We all, like, went out to...
They said,

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:38.831
"We're doing a talk-back
at a bar around the corner."

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:41.101
And it was just an excuse
for us to, like,

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.601
just talk and hang out.
-That's so nice.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:43.836
So, I'm assuming
when they reached out

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.338
and said, "Bowen,
we'd like you to play God,"

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.873
It was a quick yes.
-Quick yes.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.241
And I'm really honored.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.576
It's like, what, me,
Morgan Freeman,

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.511
Alanis Morissette,
and George Burns?

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:55.281
Like, that's a crazy...
-Yeah, those are the four gods.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.951
-Those are the -- That's
the Mount Rushmore of gods.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.487
We're like the "Sex and
the City" girls of Gods.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:04.590
-How -- I mean, I know
you always do a lot of research

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.925
about a character
before you play it.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:08.560
What did you find
that drew you to God?

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.231
-Well, I read the entire Bible
cover to cover,

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.133
and in Aramaic.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:17.302
[ Laughter ]
No, I...I...

00:02:17.302 --> 00:02:21.640
So, God in this movie is this,
like, really petulant

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.543
sort of gay entity.

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:26.880
And it got me thinking,
like, my way in was like,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.049
God is kind of a messy queen,
you know?

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:34.553
Like, he's so dramatic,
floods the world,

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:37.123
makes it rain frogs.
That's campy.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.624
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.960
Like, you know,
the whole Book of Job is him,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.597
like, playing The Sims
on this one guy, like...

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.366
You know?

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:49.435
So, I feel like that is --
this is a very, like,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.704
it's a "new" portrayal of God,
but it's like, it's God

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.172
the way we understand God.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.041
-Yes, that we haven't
been able to admit

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.543
that's what God
has been telling us.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.244
-Exactly.
-And now you're finally like,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.679
let's just own it.
-And let's just own it.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.749
Everyone's free to just call God
a messy queen from now on.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.216
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:05.885
This is a great cast.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.186
Nathan Lane.
-Yes.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:08.421
-Megan Mullally is in it.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.055
-But really all anybody

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:11.723
who's seen the movie
is talking about is,

00:03:11.723 --> 00:03:13.492
is the sewer boys.
-The sewer boys.

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:15.328
-So, the sewer boys
are these two characters

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.797
that belong to Nathan Lane
in the film.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.532
-Yep. That's right.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.134
-They're, like,
just prosthetic dudes.

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:24.337
-Yes, they're real puppets.
They're prosthetic dudes.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.005
-Here's a good sense of
their actual size.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.173
-That's right.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:30.009
So, that's them with us
on the red carpet.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.343
I...

00:03:31.343 --> 00:03:35.315
Someone made me hold one of them
on the red carpet,

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.183
and I wasn't --
I thought they were

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.384
really adorable, really cute.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.888
But then when I touched them,
they're...

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.356
Whoever made them,

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:48.660
made them out of, like, real
skin and bone, it seemed like.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.329
I was like, this is vile.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.597
But I'm curious --

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.065
You've lived in New York
a long time.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:55.401
Do you believe that
there is, like, a species,

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.171
a lateral species
of, like, sewer people?

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.105
Like, mole people?
What do you think?

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:01.340
-100%.
-Yes!

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.676
-Yeah. 100%.
-There has to be.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.344
-And I think they're not
that upset about it.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:06.345
-No.
-Yeah.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:07.546
-Great real estate down there.

00:04:07.546 --> 00:04:09.682
-Yeah. I think they're great.
Like, absolutely.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.350
They have so much space
and they're, like...

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.286
-It's by the train.
-It's by the train.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:15.821
Talking about God,
you actually, as a kid,

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.957
wanted to make a deal
with the devil.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.291
-Yes, I think...

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:23.796
I guess I admitted this
on a press thing for this movie.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.164
Someone unlocked
a memory for me.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.332
They said, "Did you ever sell...

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.667
Have you ever sold your soul
to the devil?"

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.502
I said, "Wait a minute,
I did!"

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:30.836
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:33.505
When I was like 11 years old,

00:04:33.505 --> 00:04:35.507
there was an episode of
"The Simpsons" that was on.

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:37.176
It's called
"Bart Sells His Soul."

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.978
Season seven, episode four,

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.614
and written by Greg Daniels,

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:44.517
who we all know and love
from "The Office."

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.318
And Bart basically sells
his soul to Milhouse,

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:47.987
and then I think by the end
of the episode, he, like,

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.922
you know, asks Satan
to give it back.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.624
And I was -- I watched that
in my basement,

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.460
being like, "You can do that?
Great!"

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.961
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.961 --> 00:04:58.464
-So, you did not watch the
episode as a cautionary tale.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:03.302
-No, no. Purely encouraged.
And just had, like,

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:05.304
an imaginary conversation
with Satan.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.306
I think I just wanted
to play, like, a video game.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.575
I think I just wanted to play,
like, ironically,

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:12.077
like Diablo 2 or something.

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:14.580
And I got it, and I...

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.416
And so he upheld his bargain,
and I think

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:19.585
I'm still technically
locked into this deal.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.086
-You seem fine, though.

00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:24.690
-I don't know, I feel like
I come off soulless sometimes.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.360
Right, guys?
But I blame Greg Daniels

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.495
for this Faustian
bargain, though.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.731
-Yeah, well, you've got to
pin it on somebody.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.232
You might as well pin it on him.
-He owes me a show.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.668
-Yeah, there you go.
Did you...Do you have any...

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.504
You know, I know, five months
of not doing "SNL."

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.139
Are there any sketches
you've come up with

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.808
over the years
that you have pitched

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.575
that you wish
had been received better?

00:05:43.575 --> 00:05:46.713
-Oh, yeah. I mean,
just always, always, always.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:51.117
But the one that I think really,
really, like, got away from me

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:54.653
was Jenna Ortega was here last
season, and at Monday pitch,

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:59.192
I pitched her this thing where
she is a children's book author

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:04.097
and she writes a book
that's kind of like

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:05.431
"Can You Give a Mouse a Cookie."

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.032
-"Can You Give a Mouse a Cookie"
is a great book.

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:08.534
-Great book.
-And it's about how things just

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.068
get, like, sort of...
You give a mouse a cookie

00:06:10.068 --> 00:06:11.470
and that's just the beginning
of the problem, yeah.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.805
-Just the beginning
of a problem.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:16.509
And I pitched her
a children's book title

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:18.844
that she could be
the author of, called

00:06:18.844 --> 00:06:20.680
"Can You Give a Bitch a Break?"

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.014
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:25.851
And, didn't take.
Didn't take.

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:27.653
-How could that not take?
-I know! I don't know.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.254
-They've lost their minds
up there!

00:06:29.254 --> 00:06:30.923
-Exactly.
-Hey, thanks for being back.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.925
-Thanks for having me, Seth.
-I'm so happy "SNL" is back.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:35.094
I'm so happy you're back
in the building.

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:36.261
Bowen Yang!

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:39.398
"SNL" premieres Saturday
on NBC and Peacock.

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:41.134
"Dicks: The Musical"
is in select theaters now

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:42.301
and nationwide October 20th.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.570 line:0%
We'll be right back
with Jason Blum.

